# Fixed defect 132's class, 2026-09-29, a block's head alone over a line at
# its own margin (the limit lane 132 named). Symptom: `for` alone over a
# same-margin `print(3)` reported the missing body, and `if`, `while`,
# `else if` and a bound `match` alone over the same line did not: two
# heads, one mistake, told for one of them and silent for the others. Both
# readings agree the body is missing, at different offsets: read apart, the
# head's line ends at the break and the body is missing at the `print`;
# joined, the line runs on and the parser holds the missing body back at the
# end of the block, as a join's. `for` alone was told only because the joined
# `for print(3)` also refused its loop variable. Cause: `parse/apart` asked
# only whether the joined reading had refused something before the apart
# reading's report, never whether the two readings said the same report of
# the same head. Now a missing body the apart reading says at the first word
# of the line below a break, and the joined one holds farther along that
# line, is the author's mistake, told once, where the lines put it
# (`agreed`). The control arm, `check --permissive`, reads the join as the
# program and says the joined reading's report, as it did.

function an_if_alone()
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    if
    print(1)  #~ missing_body

function a_while_alone()
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    while
    print(2)  #~ missing_body

function a_for_alone()
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    for
    print(3)  #~ missing_body

function an_else_if_alone(n: i64)
    if n > 0
        print(0)
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    else if
    print(4)  #~ missing_body

function a_match_alone() -> i64
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    k = match
    print(5)  #~ missing_match_arms
    return 0

function an_if_left_open(a: i64)
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    if a >
    print(6)  #~ missing_body
    print(7)

function main()
    an_if_alone()
    a_while_alone()
    a_for_alone()
    an_else_if_alone(n: 1)
    print(a_match_alone())
    an_if_left_open(a: 1)
